le C has strong decision quality and attention, his egocentric attitude and lack of adaptability are bigger concerns. So B remains best.\n\nThus public message: I acknowledge the lack of direct decision quality evidence for B and note the attention accuracy concern (weak memory for numbers). However, B's high reliability, stress resilience, technical competence still outweigh. I maintain recommendation for B.\n\nNow produce metadata with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
